  "essentialSource": {
    "url": "https://students.uu.nl/media/29242",
    "observedLink": "Direct naar → Onderwijs- en Examenregeling (OER) B&O Bachelor on the current official regulations landing page.",
    "identity": "OER Bachelor Bestuurs- en organisatiewetenschap 2026–2027, article 1.1 applies to this academic year; full PDF body read, not a search excerpt.",
    "sha256": "143011ec85c389089fc869156bcb3acf233daceb62acc8e0c8e929d2efe3df1c",
    "sections": {
      "3.1–3.5": "Public governance, organisations, research and professional action; supporting disciplines; Dutch with English teaching; 180 EC, 142.5 EC major, at least 37.5 level-2 and 45 level-3 major EC; 22.5 EC individual final project. Social/professional skills embedded, mandatory attendance, no extra credits.",
      "3.5.3": "For entrants from September 2020: 15 EC in an international context across major and profiling; English teaching AND English assessment, or study at a foreign institution. Required English institutions course contributes 7.5 EC. Exchange briefing’s profiling 7.5 EC does not contradict the degree-wide 15 EC.",
      "3.6–3.8": "37.5 EC genuine profiling; at least 15 EC level 3 for this cohort. Board may deduct credits proportionally for whole or partial overlap, including study elsewhere. Overseas courses require prior approval. No automatic blanket prohibition or extra imaginary credits.",
      "4.2": "USG2020 after passing USG1030 AND USG1050; USG3031 after USG2090 AND USG2010; graduation after USG2020. Catalogue desired background is additional, not a waiver. Current course titles differ from legacy shorthand but codes identify same courses.",
      "4.3": "Unconditional year-three entry after all year-one and year-two courses. Board discretion after all year one and at least 45 EC year two, or more than 30 and less than 45 with limited-course study contract. These are discretionary exceptions, not guaranteed progression.",
      "4.4": "Major is reserved to admitted major students except specified exchange provisions. Own B&O(Plus) minors and USG5520 are excluded; genuine profiling remains open.",
      "5.3": "Individual graduation research with supervisor and second assessor, minimum 5.5; no invented dated deadlines from the older handbook.",
      "Annex 1": "Eight first-year 7.5 EC courses =60; year two major 52.5 plus profiling 7.5=60; year three major 30 including capstone 7.5 and thesis 22.5, plus profiling30=60. Overall major142.5+profiling37.5=180."
    }
  },
